22:00 | QUESTION  | Q-2026-08-12-4: FFT determinism vs parity — rustfft's
                    wasm_simd feature changes fp operation order. Keep it OFF
                    for byte-stable parity, or accept a documented |Δ| bound
                    like the existing libm tail? Default decision in plan: OFF.
22:00 | QUESTION  | Q-2026-08-12-5: usearch (C++ FFI, spec-normative §5.3) vs
                    pure-Rust HNSW — usearch does not compile to
                    wasm32-unknown-unknown and may not be bit-deterministic
                    across platforms. Plan decision: VectorIndex trait; pure-
                    Rust HNSW default (deterministic, seeded); usearch behind
                    native-only `usearch` feature flag. Does TLC/parity
                    evidence need a determinism proof for the index, or is the
                    index outside the discrete Spec surface (retrieval order
                    only feeds Match policy)?
22:00 | QUESTION  | Q-2026-08-12-6: candle (spec-normative §4.1) is f32-first;
                    core Φ math is f64 with 1e-10 energy checks. Plan decision:
                    core Φ stays hand-rolled f64; candle enters at the readout/
                    training-serving layer (decoupled by 𝔸5, so precision
                    cannot touch Inv1–4). Is a candle-accelerated Predictor
                    (native feature) worth the parity risk in v0.2.0, or defer
                    to v0.3.0?
